I'm using this folder to explore the syntax structure before I update the parser.

For each behavior, there is a meaning. It is composed of behaviors which keep decomposing until it reaches the atomic meaning. The further up you go in the tree, there is more meaning and the further down you go, there is less meaning. Although, saying less meaning doesn't make it less valuable, its just that as you go higher up, more meaning is compressed into a smaller representation.

So in my UI, I need to allow the user to be able to click on a behavior and expand into its composite meaning. This way the recursive meaning can be visualized interactively. Each level of recursion will load a new file that establishes that behavior.

```
Design
└── Behavior
    ├── Behavior
    │   ├── Atomic Transformation
    │   ├── Atomic Transformation
    │   └── Atomic Transformation
    │
    ├── Behavior
    │   ├── Atomic Transformation
    │   └── Atomic Transformation
    │
    └── Behavior
        ├── Atomic Transformation
        └── Atomic Transformation
```

So in my syntax, I am planning on exhibiting behavior, which is imported. It keeps decomposing until it reaches atomic and as you go up the nesting you reach the design. 

The behaviors can be reused in the design using this approach.

```
design designName{
    behavior initializeWorldState{
        // create participants
        select(A1)
    }
    behavior A1{
        exhibitBehavior(compositeBehavior)
        select(B1)
    }
    behavior B1{

    }
    run(A1)
}
```

```
design("designName")

behavior compositeBehavior{
    behavior A2{
        atomicTransformation()
        select(B)
    }
    behavior B2{

    }
    run(A2)
}
```

This approach is far more scalable, behaviors can be reused in the design.